  "verbalization": "Garcinone E is shown to have a target relationship with Raji, which in turn is targeted by multiple compounds, including Diosmetin 7-O-Beta-D-Glucopyranosyl-(1->2)-Beta-D-Glucopyranosyl-(1->2)-[Alpha-L-Rhamnopyranosyl-(1->6)]-Beta-D-Glucopyranoside and Maplexin A. Both of these compounds are linked to U373 MG, suggesting a potential mechanism of action involving the targeting of Raji cells by Garcinone E. The evidence implies that Garcinone E may act through a pathway that involves the modulation of cellular processes in Raji cells, which are subsequently targeted by other compounds, ultimately leading to the inhibition of U373 MG. The integration of these pathways highlights a possible role for Garcinone E in targeting Raji cells, which may be a key step in the broader mechanism of action against U373 MG.",
